			<div class="content" id="post-content-2814564">
									

<p>Hmm, is the wall of the room qualifies as &quot;object&quot;? If not how about stuff attached/part of the wall but not necessarily function as the wall i.e. light switch or embedded nails? what about the container of the liquid? stuff submerged within same liquid? Is opening a hole, i.e. to drop objects within the chamber, qualifies as expanding the enclosed space? what if something is connected via cable i.e. CCTV cameras? is the cable qualifies as object along with the camera?</p>
<p>The vague definition of what qualifies as &quot;Objects&quot; and &quot;Enclosed space&quot; break the article a bit for me&#8230; although it's pretty good concept IMO. no vote for now&#8230;</p>

